<title>CHINA: Rhone-Poulenc finalises Shanghai land.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc finalises Shanghai land.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>French pharmaceutical and chemical group Rhone-Poulenc has completed acquisition of a 20-hectare site in Shanghai on which it will build facilities valued at $20 million, a company statement said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said the site in a development zone in the Minhang southwest area of Shanghai's city centre would include silicon workshops and warehouses.</p>
<p>The company's investments in China so far total $300 million divided between 13 joint ventures and wholly-owned enterprises employing around 1,400 people, the statement added.</p>
</text>
